# BHL search terms — the names the OLDER literature published under.
#
# TEMPLATE. Copy to `bhl_terms.yaml` and rewrite for the clade.
#
# These are deliberately NOT the OpenAlex queries. BHL indexes pre-1930
# material, and that literature used names that are now synonyms, segregate
# genera, or superseded combinations. Searching BHL for only the current
# accepted name is the single most common way to miss the historical half of a
# library.
#
# Plain search terms, not filter syntax — BHL takes a `searchterm`.
#
# Measured, on siphonophores:
#   Bargmannia   catalogue 1 part   | full-text 9 hits  -> 4 parts
#   Stephanomia  catalogue 0 parts  | full-text 554 hits -> 29 parts
#
# Note the second row. `Stephanomia` is a historical name and returns *nothing*
# by catalogue search — the 29 parts exist only in full text. That is the case
# for `--fulltext`, and the 525 non-Part hits it also returned (whole volumes,
# dropped automatically) are the case for it being opt-in and capped.
#
# So: put current names here for the catalogue pass, and expect the historical
# ones to need `--fulltext` to surface at all.

# --- Current accepted name ---
- Viburnum

# --- Segregate genera the 19th-century literature published under. Ørsted
# split Viburnum into these; a paper about V. tinus may only ever say
# "Tinus laurifolius". ---
- Oreinotinus
- Solenotinus
- Lentago
- Tinus
- Opulus
- Microtinus
- Thyrsosma

# --- Family names that formerly contained the genus ---
- Caprifoliaceae
